  "source": "session study tvlfactors/ (scratchpad): snaps_all.tsv = pool-memory position snapshots (one per management cycle, ~3 min), perf.jsonl = perf records; extract script tvldistress/extract.py",
  "readings": "Each reading is one pool-memory snapshot of the position: tvl_usd = the snapshot's pool_tvl (detail.tvl of the same pool-discovery row the TVL exit reads), volume_usd = pool_volume (the row's windowed `volume` at the screening timeframe 1h, so turnover scale factor 1), pnl_pct = the snapshot's pnl_pct (assumed management-ready and usable \u2014 readiness flags are not in the snapshots), active_bin = the snapshot's active bin.",
  "entry_bin": "DERIVED: the active bin of the position's FIRST pool-memory snapshot (entry_bin_source first_snapshot). For bot deploys and adopted positions the live code reads active_bin_at_deploy (the deploy bin / the adopting scan's bin), which is the same or one cycle earlier. wifout-SOL 4fz7zmt7's series does not start at entry (entry_tvl 0 on its record), so its entry bin is the first snapshot available \u2014 its loss leg (PnL \u221240 %) decides anyway.",
  "bin_step": "from the perf record (binstep).",
  "timing": "The TVL streak and the distress streak are replayed with the live pure functions on the snapshot timestamps, with the on-chain cross-check assumed to agree. Live ready moments' readings end AT the ready reading (the position closed there); WINSTON 4C4jzy4R and the historical collapses continue after the TVL proof (they were not closed by it).",
  "kinds": "false_close = the 10 live TVL-exit closes of 2026-11-22 \u2026 11-28 the operator called not real collapses; real_live = PVE 4sXgrxZt (closed by the rule 11-26, pool at $349 two hours later) and WINSTON 4C4jzy4R (ready 11-27 15:51 and again 17:18 UTC, held/hands-off, pool died); historical = the 7 collapses of the study (DUST, ART \u00d73, FACTORY, SAPIJIJU, wifout), ready moment = the first 3-reading/5-min TVL proof of their series.",
  "thresholds": "The rule's thresholds (\u221210 % loss, \u221230 % price fallback, turnover 2, price \u22125 %) were chosen on these same cases \u2014 the fixture shows the rule reproduces its own study, nothing more."
 },
